ld be with my teammate or in the unseen deck — but more likely with landlord since they only have 3 cards. If landlord has RedJoker, they’d beat my BlackJoker and be down to 2 cards, then could play a pair and win.\n\n**Passing** might be safest if I think teammate can handle later, but they passed earlier, so they might not have a high single. Letting landlord take this trick with just an A means they’ll have 2 cards — possibly a pair that wins immediately.\n\nBest choice: **Beat with ♥2**. It’s high enough that landlord likely can’t beat it (unless they have a Joker or last 2), and I keep BlackJoker for later. This also communicates to my teammate that I have high strength, possibly enabling them to conserve cards.\n\n**Reason:**  \nWith landlord at 3 cards, taking control with ♥2 is less risky than using BlackJoker (preserves highest card), and better than passing (which gives landlord a free trick). My teammate’s pass suggests weakness, so I should act.\n\n**Answer:**  \n{"cards": ["♥2"]}'}
